\tag{fdip}
\title{Cyclic gauge fields and dual flux sectors}
\date{2026-11-11}

\p{The [finite surface character formula](fdip-006W) sums
representation labels after the links have been averaged.
For a cyclic group, the labels themselves add modulo the group
order. In higher dimensions their cancellation at each link
leaves closed surfaces, which can wind around the periodic
directions. How do these surfaces become fields on the dual
lattice, and how does a Wilson loop change their boundary?}

\p{The [finite Fourier transform](fdip-000S) supplies the
local change of variables. Its ring-valued version below keeps
the character orthogonality hypothesis explicit. The resulting
finite sums retain every torus flux sector.}

